hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15639","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Umari narrated to us, Abu Sahl Awf ibn Abi Jamilah narrated to us, from Zayd Abu al-Qamus, from the delegation of Abd al-Qays, that they heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: O Allah, make us among Your chosen servants, the radiant with ablution marks, the accepted delegation. He said: So they said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the chosen servants of Allah. He said: The righteous servants of Allah. They said: Who are the radiant with ablution marks. He said: Those whose places of purification whiten from them. They said: Who are the accepted delegation. He said: A delegation that comes from this nation with their Prophet to their Lord, Blessed and Exalted."
